  "description": "Rich crimson vintage bird and holly surface pattern inspired by William Morris Arts and Crafts design.\nThis striking repeating pattern features song thrushes perched among densely layered holly branches, acanthus-style scrolling foliage, and clusters of vivid red berries set against a deep crimson red background. The botanical elements combine spiky holly leaves rendered in sage green and slate blue-grey with curling golden-tan acanthus fronds, while cream-white small flowers and pale berry clusters add delicate contrast. The illustrative linework is engraving-style, giving every leaf and feather a hand-drawn, antique etched quality that evokes 19th-century textile heritage.\nThe mood is richly festive yet refined — opulent without being kitsch, making it ideal for premium Christmas and holiday design projects. The deep red, olive green, steel blue, warm tan, and cream colour palette feels both traditional and elevated, working beautifully for fabric design, gift wrap, holiday stationery, scrapbooking paper, Christmas card backgrounds, sublimation printing, and POD products such as tote bags, mugs, wrapping paper, and throw pillows. The pattern tiles seamlessly at 13×13 inches at 300 DPI, making it production-ready for Spoonflower, Redbubble, Printify, Canva, Procreate, and Photoshop workflows.",
  "fullDescription": "<p>Rich crimson vintage bird and holly surface pattern inspired by William Morris Arts and Crafts design.</p>\n<p>This striking repeating pattern features song thrushes perched among densely layered holly branches, acanthus-style scrolling foliage, and clusters of vivid red berries set against a deep crimson red background. The botanical elements combine spiky holly leaves rendered in sage green and slate blue-grey with curling golden-tan acanthus fronds, while cream-white small flowers and pale berry clusters add delicate contrast. The illustrative linework is engraving-style, giving every leaf and feather a hand-drawn, antique etched quality that evokes 19th-century textile heritage.</p>\n<p>The mood is richly festive yet refined — opulent without being kitsch, making it ideal for premium Christmas and holiday design projects. The deep red, olive green, steel blue, warm tan, and cream colour palette feels both traditional and elevated, working beautifully for fabric design, gift wrap, holiday stationery, scrapbooking paper, Christmas card backgrounds, sublimation printing, and POD products such as tote bags, mugs, wrapping paper, and throw pillows. The pattern tiles seamlessly at 13×13 inches at 300 DPI, making it production-ready for Spoonflower, Redbubble, Printify, Canva, Procreate, and Photoshop workflows.</p>",
